// Laws the shipped systems do not have: itemized deductions and the child tax
// credit, at the end of the year, feeding the forked `us` in systems/us.ax.
//
// FILE ORDER MATTERS. Laws that fire at year end run in the order their files are
// read, which is path order: this file (laws.ax) sorts before systems/us.ax, so it
// tallies `itemized` and `credits` before the forked federal-income-tax reads them.
// Rename this file `tax.ax` and it sorts after, and every figure here changes.

/// Schedule A: mortgage interest (IRC §163(h)), state and local taxes up to the
/// cap (IRC §164(b)(6)), and gifts to charity (IRC §170), for the year that
/// just ended. `us` takes the larger of this and the standard deduction. The
/// State tax counted is what was withheld plus last year's balance paid, and
/// the property tax the servicer paid from escrow.
law itemized-deductions
  each year
  let salt = min(tally(salt) + tally(ca-withheld), salt-cap[year])
  count tally(mortgage-interest) + salt + tally(charity) as itemized

/// The child tax credit (IRC §24): 2,200 USD for each qualifying child under 17,
/// phased out above 400,000 USD of income on a joint return (not modelled: this
/// household is far below it).
law child-tax-credit
  each year
  count child-tax-credit[year] * owner.children as credits


// ─── Figures ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// The dependent-care FSA cap (IRC §129(a)(2)). 2026 rises to 7,500 (P.L. 119-21).
param dependent-care-limit
  2024 5_000 USD
  2025 5_000 USD
  2026 7_500 USD

// The cap on the state and local tax deduction (IRC §164(b)(6), P.L. 119-21).
// verify: the 2026 figure.
param salt-cap
  2024 10_000 USD
  2025 40_000 USD
  2026 40_400 USD

// The child tax credit per child (IRC §24, P.L. 119-21).
param child-tax-credit
  2024 2_000 USD
  2025 2_200 USD
  2026 2_200 USD
